Subject: resolver: on OpenVMS, close a tracking file before deleting it

DefaultTrackingFileManager.delete() opens the tracking file (*.lastUpdated,
_remote.repositories), locks it, and deletes it while the channel is still
open. Unix lets a process delete an open file, and the JDK on Windows opens
files with FILE_SHARE_DELETE, but OpenVMS refuses: Files.delete() fails with
"file currently locked by another user", so every artifact download ended in
an UncheckedIOException and the build failed.

On OpenVMS take the lock as before (it still waits out another Maven process
that is writing the file), release it and close the file, then delete. The
window between the two is the same one a Maven process on Windows has had
with older JDKs. Other systems keep the upstream behaviour.

Fits upstream (apache/maven-resolver) as an os.name check; to be offered there.

--- a/vmsport/src/maven-resolver-impl/org/eclipse/aether/internal/impl/DefaultTrackingFileManager.java	2026-11-06 20:14:59.226193062 +0000
+++ b/vmsport/src/maven-resolver-impl/org/eclipse/aether/internal/impl/DefaultTrackingFileManager.java	2026-11-06 20:14:59.231838996 +0000
@@ -120,13 +120,24 @@
         }
     }
 
+    private static final boolean IS_OPENVMS =
+            System.getProperty("os.name", "").toLowerCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT).startsWith("openvms");
+
     @Override
     public boolean delete(File file) {
         Path path = file.toPath();
         if (Files.isReadable(path)) {
             synchronized (mutex(path)) {
-                try (FileChannel fileChannel = FileChannel.open(path, StandardOpenOption.WRITE);
-                        FileLock unused = fileLock(fileChannel, false)) {
+                try {
+                    // OpenVMS cannot delete a file that is still open, so take the
+                    // lock to wait out other writers, release it, then delete.
+                    try (FileChannel fileChannel = FileChannel.open(path, StandardOpenOption.WRITE);
+                            FileLock unused = fileLock(fileChannel, false)) {
+                        if (!IS_OPENVMS) {
+                            Files.delete(path);
+                            return true;
+                        }
+                    }
                     Files.delete(path);
                     return true;
                 } catch (NoSuchFileException e) {
